  "confidence": "high",
  "notes": "Sourced from Midas's official \"PRO SERIES / PRO X-CC-IP\" datasheet (Midas-branded PDF, mirrored by AV retailer BZB Express; midasconsoles.com no longer hosts a live PRO X product page for this discontinued/legacy Pro Series line). \"PRO X-CC-IP\" is the current designation for the control-centre/control-surface half of the system marketed as \"Midas PRO X\" — a separate DL251 audio engine/stage box (rack-mounted, sold separately) provides most of the actual stage-side mic/line I/O and is NOT covered by this datasheet or port list. The console itself is a large console/desk unit (1365 x 940 x 434 mm), not rack-mountable, so rackUnits is omitted. Individual numbered port names (Mic/Line In 1-8, AES50 1-3, AES3 In/Out 1-4, Line Out 1-8, etc.) reflect quantities given in the spec sheet; exact printed rear-panel labels (e.g. \"A/B\" vs \"1/2/3\" for AES50, \"X/Y\" redundancy pairing) could not be independently confirmed from this document. Snake (Fibre) ports use Neutrik opticalCON DUO connectors, mapped to the closest available id \"fiber-lc\". KVM Input (qty 3) is modeled as a VGA video-in port paired with a USB-A port for keyboard/mouse pass-through, per the spec's \"Analogue VGA, USB keyboard & mouse\" description — exact USB connector gender/count per KVM input is not stated. No bandwidth grade was set on AES50/etherCON digital-audio links, the HyperMAC copper snake, or the \"Ethernet Control Data\"/\"External Ethernet Tunnel\" ports because the spec states audio channel count/format rather than a stated Ethernet PHY speed. USB Interface ports are graded usb-2.0 per the stated \"USB 2.0 full speed (12.0 Mbit/s)\" spec. Three hot-swappable, N+1-redundant power-supply modules (MKT-PSU-2) each have their own IEC mains inlet (100-240 VAC).",
